<div class="kh-content kh-collage-rules">
<h2>What transfers</h2>
<p>Use a few unequal cuts and a clear centre of gravity. Preserve wide paper gaps between fragments. Let actual project imagery supply the detail; keep captions, controls and the meaningful screenshot intact.</p>
<h2>Where it belongs</h2>
<p>A selected work cover, a redesign article illustration or an occasional social card. Keep ordinary index thumbnails, reading pages, code, navigation and photographs in their current treatments. Avoid a second set of decorative shards around the homepage’s existing disc and project plate.</p>
<h2>Reference and credit</h2>
<p>The reference is the TurboGrafx-16 advertisement supplied in this conversation. Its printed NEC and TurboGrafx-16 marks identify the product; the scan does not establish its date, publication, agency or designer, so those credits remain unverified. No advertising artwork, faces, game screenshots or branding from that scan are used here. The composition uses an existing screenshot from Ken’s Mangrove case study and original CSS shapes.</p>
</div>
</article>
